%% A parameter the call binds to an input type, and a parameter the callee's
%% clauses fix, in one instantiation (TGLP, parameterized-types.tex,
%% Definition "Instantiation": a map under which the caller's clause and the
%% clauses of the callee are well-typed).  The reader C? at X binds X to
%% Choice?, the caller's clause admitting no other polarity there; D occurs
%% first in this call, so nothing in go fixes M, and pass's clause does: the
%% pair A, A? must be dual, and with A at Choice? that makes the type at M?
%% Choice, so M is Choice?.  The instantiation is pass(Choice?, Choice), under
%% which pass(A, A?) is well-typed.  Probing pass's clause with X at its output
%% type instead gives M = Choice, and pass(Choice?, Choice?) makes neither
%% clause well-typed.
%% Fixture of glp_runtime/test/analysis/input_binding_callee_test.dart.

Choice ::= yes ; no.

procedure(X, M) pass(X, M?).
pass(A, A?).

procedure use(Choice?, Choice).
use(C, C?).

procedure go(Choice?, Choice).
go(C, E?) :- pass(C?, D), use(D?, E).
